{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'tail -n 150 /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1790831000000-engineer-linker-L4.claude-opus-5-5.stdout.log'","aggregated_output":"# Engineer report: linker over dao.jing.dht, slice L4\n\nL4 is implemented and every lane passed when run in the foreground. Each acceptance bullet has a test, and I demonstrated failing runs (missing implementation or mutations) before green. Nothing is staged or committed. One spec gap needs an Architect decision (finding 1).\n\nReport file: `collab/1790812000000-engineer-linker-L4.claude-opus-5-5.report.md`. Worktree `datomworld-linker-l2`, branch `linker-l4`, from `bd9bfae7`.\n\n| Lane | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `clj -M:kondo --lint` on all 13 changed src/test files | 0 errors, 0 warnings |\n| `bb test:clj` | 2683 tests, 224122 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n| `bb test:cljs` | 2597 tests, 90245 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors; all 6 changed namespaces ran |\n| `bb build:yin-repl-peer` | built; its warnings are all in files I didn't touch |\n| `bb test:cljd` (after `rm -rf test/cljd-out`) | `+2552 … All tests passed!`; the 11 new tests are in the regenerated suite |\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`yin.vm.linker.publish`:** `module-from-index` derives a module from indexed code (5.3). `assertion`, `retraction`, `next-seq` and `name-envelopes` sign the name claims; the next sequence is derived from the publisher's own index (6.1, 6.5, 6.6).\n- **`yin.vm.linker.dht`:**\n  - The snapshot set is now HEAD plus every loaded index (7.2).\n  - New `authority` helper.\n  - New `resolve-name` gives the section 9 refusal shapes for names.\n  - New `publish-name!` is the single plain call behind publishing: derive, publish, sign.\n- **`yin.repl.index`:** every evaluated program's rows go into the index store each round (5.1). A failed row write records stage `:materialize` and the round doesn't publish. `commit-names` commits the signed envelopes as one transaction and publishes at once, so HEAD announces them.\n- **`yin.repl.link` / `yin.repl` / `yin.repl.query`:** the reader's declared principals, plus its own key's principal, reach the link source. A new `yin.link` host module answers `publish` and `names`. Each call checks its arguments and makes one plain call. The session's indexer then commits the envelopes. No REPL code walks, fetches, folds or signs.\n- **`yin.repl.main`:**\n  - New flags `--dht-key`, `--dht-principal` (strict 64-char lowercase hex) and `--dht-keygen`.\n  - Key loading never falls back to a fresh key.\n  - Keygen never overwrites an existing file, and the seed is never printed.\n  - Banner lines added; all three hosts' `-main` handle keygen.\n- **Docs:** `yin.vm.linker.dht.md` (5.3 options, section 10 rows) and `yin.repl.dao.space-index.md` (rows every round, names as one transaction).\n\n## Acceptance bullets → evidence\n\n1. **Rows each round; a second node loads the tree by its root.** `every-row-of-each-evaluated-program-is-in-the-index-store` and `every-round-s-rows-are-published-and-a-second-node-loads-the-tree-by-its-root`.\n2. **More rows than the pending-write bound, acknowledged, never `/busy`, eight rounds in a row.** `rounds-larger-than-the-pending-write-bound-are-acknowledged-never-busy`.\n3. **A failed row replication.** `a-failed-row-is-partial-unreachable-except-from-the-publisher-and-repaired`:\n   - The round is `:partial`, naming exactly that row, and HEAD moved.\n   - The first line names the result, \"1 of N blobs not sent\", and that the node is retrying.\n   - A reader that can't reach the publisher fails `:miss` on that row; one that can, loads it.\n   - After healing, the node repairs on its own after at least 30000 ticks, prints the acknowledged line, and a new load succeeds.\n   - `retry-at-the-prompt-brings-the-same-repair-forward` covers `(dao.space.dht/retry m)`.\n4. **Refused manifest.** `a-refused-manifest-is-unacknowledged-and-repaired-the-same-way`.\n5. **Peers that never accept.** `with-peers-that-never-accept-twenty-rounds-report-and-the-ticker-idles`: 20 first reports, no acknowledgement, every prompt answers at once, and the ticker goes idle again after a repair cycle.\n6. **Module published in a `:partial` round.** `a-module-published-in-a-partial-round-is-absent-until-repaired`: the reader resolves the name, the require is refused `:absent` with the miss cause, and after repair it evaluates to `4242`.\n7. **Two-principal dependency at the prompt.** `a-two-principal-dependency-evaluates-or-raises-dependency-binding`: `:absent`, then evaluates to `43`, then `:mismatch`, then `:ambiguous`.\n8. **`(yin.link/publish 'my.lib '[f])`.** `publish-at-the-prompt-derives-one-tree-and-declares-what-it-reads` and `publish-at-the-prompt-refuses-and-writes-nothing`, plus plain tests showing a refusal leaves the store at zero entries.\n9. **Republishing a name.** `republishing-a-name-retracts-then-asserts-…` and `republishing-a-name-resolves-by-the-snapshot-a-reader-holds` (new snapshot gives the new address, old gives the old, both give the new).\n10. **The fold over the snapshot set.** `the-fold-reports-what-does-not-resolve-and-refuses-ambiguity`, plus L2's `an-envelope-in-two-snapshots-is-one-event`.\n11. **Only HEAD and loaded indexes are folded.** `only-head-and-loaded-indexes-are-folded`.\n12. **Key file cases.** Three `main-test` tests: missing, malformed and mismatched files each refuse startup; keygen refuses to overwrite; the seed appears in no output.\n13. **Sequence after a restart.** `the-next-sequence-is-derived-from-the-index-after-a-restart` writes seqs 1, 2, 3, so there is no equivocation.\n\n## Failing runs before green, and mutations\n\n- **Before the implementation:** the `publish` and `linker.dht` tests failed with `No such var`. The index tests failed with 15 failures and 1 error. The 6 new REPL/main tests failed with 22 failures and 2 errors.\n- **Mutations, all caught and restored (`cmp`-checked):**\n\n  | # | Mutation | Caught by |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | M1 | rows not materialized | 4 tests: 27 failures, 1 error |\n  | M2 | HEAD left out of the snapshot set | 4 failures |\n  | M3 | earliest instead of latest defining program | 1 failure |\n  | M4 | republish writes no retraction | 6 failures |\n  | M5 | sequence always 1 | 4 failures |\n  | M6 | node doesn't declare its own principal | 2 failures |\n\n## Findings for the Architect / owner\n\n1. **Spec gap in 5.3: needs a decision.** If the publisher typed `(require 'base)` as its own program, the derived tree never runs it, because 5.3 collects only defining programs. The manifest still declares `base` under `:requires`. But the install child only passes the reader modules it actually linked, so on the reader `(app/g)` fails with `Unable to resolve symbol: base/f` (observed). I didn't invent a rule. The two-principal test types the require and the definition as one program, which 5.3 does collect. Options: 5.3 also collects each declared module's latest requiring program, or the publisher adds the requires itself.\n2. **Section 9 name refusals now have their full shapes.** The DHT source now refuses with `:absent` plus that name's `:diagnostics`, or `:ambiguous-name` with `:addresses` and `:asserters`. L3 had answered only `{:reason :absent :name n}`.\n3. **5.1 changes existing behaviour, as specified.** A store that refuses every write now fails at stage `:materialize`, not `:publish`. I updated the two existing tests that asserted the old stage (`index_test`, `query_test`). I read \"not reported indexed\" as: a `:materialize` failure skips that round's publication.\n4. **HEAD is read from disk on every fold.** `snapshots` reads `<dir>/HEAD` and its datoms each time, so the cost grows with index size.\n5. **`(reset)` drops host modules.** It drops `yin.link` and `dao.space.dht` like other host modules, so they must be required again; this tripped one of my tests.\n6. **Dart keygen permissions.** `dart:io` has no chmod, so Dart can't set owner-only permissions on the key file. The JVM uses `rw-------` where supported; Node uses mode 0600.\n7. **Where the 5.1 banner line lives.** It's in `yin.repl.main/banner`, because `yin/repl/dht.cljc` isn't on L4's file list.\n8. **Publish answer and refusals.** `(yin.link/publish …)` answers `{:module :address :links}`. Refusals are raised as the call's error under the reason keyword.\n\n## Not done / not run\n\nNothing was skipped and no sandbox blocked a lane. Kondo ran as `clj -M:kondo` (the documented form) because `clojure -M:kondo` needed approval. My temporary scratch test file is deleted; the remaining scratch files are under git-ignored `target/l4/`, and `git status` shows only the 15 intended files.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc | sed -n '430,715p'\"","aggregated_output":"   430\t  \"The canonical CBOR size of `x`, or nil when `x` is not portable data.\"\n   431\t  [x]\n   432\t  (try\n   433\t    (byte-length (cbor/encode x))\n   434\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) _ nil)))\n   435\t\n   436\t\n   437\t(defn- in-patterns\n   438\t  \"The patterns `query` declares under `:in`, nil when it declares none.\"\n   439\t  [query]\n   440\t  (if (map? query)\n   441\t    (some-> (:in query) vec)\n   442\t    (let [[marker & after] (drop-while #(not= :in %) query)]\n   443\t      (when marker (vec (take-while (complement keyword?) after))))))\n   444\t\n   445\t\n   446\t(def ^:private ast-sources\n   447\t  \"The AST relations a query names under `:in` to have the shell supply\n   448\t   them (yin.repl.ast-index).\"\n   449\t  #{'$ast '$occ})\n   450\t\n   451\t\n   452\t(defn- caller-patterns\n   453\t  \"The `:in` patterns the caller's inputs fill: every declared pattern but\n   454\t   the session's sources, the implicit index `$` and the AST relations.\"\n   455\t  [query]\n   456\t  (vec (remove #(or (= '$ %) (contains? ast-sources %)) (in-patterns query))))\n   457\t\n   458\t\n   459\t(defn- ast-patterns\n   460\t  \"The AST relations `query` names under `:in`, in declared order.\"\n   461\t  [query]\n   462\t  (filterv #(contains? ast-sources %) (in-patterns query)))\n   463\t\n   464\t\n   465\t(defn- split-args\n   466\t  \"`[inputs options]` of the arguments after the query: one input per\n   467\t   pattern of `caller-patterns`, a map among them included, then at most\n   468\t   one options map.  A refusal when the arguments do not fit.\"\n   469\t  [query args]\n   470\t  (let [n (count (caller-patterns query))\n   471\t        [inputs more] (split-at n args)]\n   472\t    (if (and (= n (count inputs))\n   473\t             (or (empty? more) (and (= 1 (count more)) (map? (first more)))))\n   474\t      [(vec inputs) (first more)]\n   475\t      (refusal ::query-failed\n   476\t               (str \"query failed: query input arity must match :in, \" n\n   477\t                    \" :in inputs and an optional options map expected, got \"\n   478\t                    (count args) \" arguments\")\n   479\t               nil))))\n   480\t\n   481\t\n   482\t(defn- with-index\n   483\t  \"`query` with the index bound to `$`, the first database input it names,\n   484\t   then the AST relations it names, in declared order.  The index is\n   485\t   implicit: a query's `:in` names only the caller's inputs, with or\n   486\t   without `$` among them, and those inputs fill the other patterns in\n   487\t   order.  A query without `:in` takes none.\"\n   488\t  [query]\n   489\t  (let [declared (in-patterns query)\n   490\t        in (-> ['$] (into (ast-patterns query)) (into (caller-patterns query)))]\n   491\t    (cond (nil? declared) query\n   492\t          (map? query) (assoc query :in in)\n   493\t          :else (let [[before [_ & after]] (split-with #(not= :in %) query)]\n   494\t                  (-> (vec before)\n   495\t                      (conj :in)\n   496\t                      (into in)\n   497\t                      (into (drop-while (complement keyword?) after)))))))\n   498\t\n   499\t\n   500\t(defn- view-of\n   501\t  \"The view the options name, or a refusal.\"\n   502\t  [options]\n   503\t  (cond\n   504\t    (nil? options) (:current views)\n   505\t\n   506\t    (not= #{:view} (set (keys options)))\n   507\t    (invalid (str \"q options must be {:view :current} or {:view :history}, got \"\n   508\t                  (pr-str options)))\n   509\t\n   510\t    (contains? views (:view options)) (get views (:view options))\n   511\t\n   512\t    :else (invalid (str \"q :view must be :current or :history, got \"\n   513\t                        (pr-str (:view options))))))\n   514\t\n   515\t\n   516\t(defn- row-count\n   517\t  \"Rows of a collected result: a relation or collection counts its\n   518\t   members, a scalar or tuple is one.\"\n   519\t  [result]\n   520\t  (if (or (set? result) (sequential? result) (nil? result))\n   521\t    (count result)\n   522\t    1))\n   523\t\n   524\t\n   525\t(defn- bounded\n   526\t  \"The collected result `run` answers, `{:ok value}`, or a refusal: a\n   527\t   query the engine rejects, a result over `limits`, or one that is not\n   528\t   portable Yin data.\"\n   529\t  [run {:keys [row-limit byte-limit]}]\n   530\t  (let [result (try\n   531\t                 {:value (run)}\n   532\t                 (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e\n   533\t                   {:refusal (refusal ::query-failed\n   534\t                                      (str \"query failed: \"\n   535\t                                           (or (ex-message e) (str e)))\n   536\t                                      nil)}))]\n   537\t    (if-let [r (:refusal result)]\n   538\t      r\n   539\t      (let [value (:value result)\n   540\t            rows (row-count value)\n   541\t            size (when (<= rows row-limit) (encoded-size value))]\n   542\t        (cond\n   543\t          (> rows row-limit)\n   544\t          (refusal ::result-limit\n   545\t                   (str \"the query result has \" rows\n   546\t                        \" rows, over the limit of \" row-limit)\n   547\t                   {::limit {:rows row-limit}})\n   548\t\n   549\t          (nil? size)\n   550\t          (refusal ::query-failed\n   551\t                   \"the query result is not portable Yin data\"\n   552\t                   nil)\n   553\t\n   554\t          (> size byte-limit)\n   555\t          (refusal ::result-limit\n   556\t                   (str \"the query result encodes to \" size\n   557\t                        \" bytes, over the limit of \" byte-limit)\n   558\t                   {::limit {:bytes byte-limit}})\n   559\t\n   560\t          :else {:ok value})))))\n   561\t\n   562\t\n   563\t(defn- evaluate\n   564\t  [db view query inputs limits]\n   565\t  (bounded #(query/collect (apply query/q query (view db) inputs)) limits))\n   566\t\n   567\t\n   568\t(defn answer\n   569\t  \"The response to one call-pair `request`, answered from `indexer`, and\n   570\t   from `ast-indexer` for a query naming `$ast` or `$occ`, under `limits`\n   571\t   (`{:row-limit n :byte-limit n}`).  Without an AST indexer such a query\n   572\t   is refused.\"\n   573\t  ([indexer limits request]\n   574\t   (answer indexer nil limits request))\n   575\t  ([indexer ast-indexer limits request]\n   576\t   (let [id (apply2/request-id request)\n   577\t         [query & more] (apply2/request-args request)\n   578\t         answer (cond\n   579\t                  (not= op (apply2/request-op request))\n   580\t                  (refusal :dao.stream.apply/unknown-operation\n   581\t                           \"No handler for operation\"\n   582\t                           nil)\n   583\t\n   584\t                  (nil? (encoded-size (apply2/request-args request)))\n   585\t                  (invalid (str \"q takes portable Yin data only: nil, booleans,\"\n   586\t                                \" numbers, strings, keywords, symbols, and\"\n   587\t                                \" vectors, lists, sets and maps of them\"))\n   588\t\n   589\t                  (not (or (vector? query) (map? query)))\n   590\t                  (invalid (str \"q expects a query vector or map, got \"\n   591\t                                (pr-str query)))\n   592\t\n   593\t                  :else\n   594\t                  (let [split (split-args query more)\n   595\t                        [inputs options] (when-not (refused? split) split)\n   596\t                        view (when-not (refused? split) (view-of options))\n   597\t                        db (when-not (or (refused? split) (refused? view))\n   598\t                             (snapshot indexer))\n   599\t                        sources (when-not (or (refused? split) (refused? view)\n   600\t                                              (refused? db))\n   601\t                                  (ast-relations ast-indexer\n   602\t                                                 (ast-patterns query)))]\n   603\t                    (cond\n   604\t                      (refused? split) split\n   605\t                      (refused? view) view\n   606\t                      (refused? db) db\n   607\t                      (refused? sources) sources\n   608\t                      :else (evaluate db view (with-index query)\n   609\t                                      (into sources inputs) limits))))]\n   610\t     (if (refused? answer)\n   611\t       {apply2/id-key id, apply2/error-key answer}\n   612\t       (apply2/success-response id (:ok answer))))))\n   613\t\n   614\t\n   615\t(defn- host-status\n   616\t  \"A load status as the host answers it: the status without its loaded\n   617\t   value, which an index load counts under `:datoms` instead.\"\n   618\t  [status]\n   619\t  (when status\n   620\t    (cond-> (dissoc status :value)\n   621\t      (and (= :loaded (:status status)) (= dht/index-kind (:kind status)))\n   622\t      (assoc :datoms (count (:value status))))))\n   623\t\n   624\t\n   625\t(defn- publication-call\n   626\t  \"`[node' answer]` of `retry!` or `cancel!` on `manifest`: `ok` answers\n   627\t   `ok`; the plain function's refusal is answered under its own code.\"\n   628\t  [node manifest f ok]\n   629\t  (try [(f node manifest) {:ok ok}]\n   630\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e\n   631\t         (if-let [code (:dao.space.dht/refused (ex-data e))]\n   632\t           [node (refusal code (ex-message e) nil)]\n   633\t           (throw e)))))\n   634\t\n   635\t\n   636\t(defn- dht-answer\n   637\t  \"The response to one `dao.space.dht` call, answered from `node` — the\n   638\t   shell's DHT node — by the `dao.space.dht` function the operation\n   639\t   names, and the node after it: `load-index` starts a load and answers\n   640\t   its status at once, never waiting; `load-status` answers the load's\n   641\t   status map; `q` answers `dao.space.dht/q` under `limits`, refused\n   642\t   until the index is loaded; `retry` and `cancel` answer `:retrying`\n   643\t   and `:cancelled`, or the plain function's refusal; `load-module`\n   644\t   starts a closure load and answers its status, and `module-status`\n   645\t   answers it without the loaded closure.  Answers\n   646\t   `[node response]`.\"\n   647\t  [node limits request]\n   648\t  (let [id (apply2/request-id request)\n   649\t        [manifest & more] (apply2/request-args request)\n   650\t        [node answer]\n   651\t        (cond\n   652\t          (nil? node)\n   653\t          [node (unavailable (str \"the shell has no DHT node; start it with \"\n   654\t                                  \"--index-store dht:<dir> and --dht-peer\"))]\n   655\t\n   656\t          (nil? (encoded-size (apply2/request-args request)))\n   657\t          [node (invalid \"dao.space.dht takes portable Yin data only\")]\n   658\t\n   659\t          (not (jing/segment-address? manifest))\n   660\t          [node (invalid (str \"dao.space.dht expects a manifest address, got \"\n   661\t                              (pr-str manifest)))]\n   662\t\n   663\t          :else\n   664\t          (case (apply2/request-op request)\n   665\t            ::dht-load-index\n   666\t            (let [node (dht/load-index node manifest)]\n   667\t              [node {:ok (:status (dht/load-status node manifest))}])\n   668\t\n   669\t            ::dht-load-status\n   670\t            [node {:ok (host-status (dht/load-status node manifest))}]\n   671\t\n   672\t            ::dht-load-module\n   673\t            (let [node (linker.dht/load-module node manifest)]\n   674\t              [node {:ok (:status (linker.dht/module-status node manifest))}])\n   675\t\n   676\t            ::dht-module-status\n   677\t            [node {:ok (host-status (linker.dht/module-status node manifest))}]\n   678\t\n   679\t            ::dht-retry\n   680\t            (publication-call node manifest dht/retry! :retrying)\n   681\t\n   682\t            ::dht-cancel\n   683\t            (publication-call node manifest dht/cancel! :cancelled)\n   684\t\n   685\t            ::dht-q\n   686\t            (let [status (dht/load-status node manifest)\n   687\t                  [query & inputs] more]\n   688\t              [node (if (= :loaded (:status status))\n   689\t                      (bounded #(apply dht/q node manifest query inputs) limits)\n   690\t                      (refusal ::index-unavailable\n   691\t                               (str \"the index \" manifest \" is not loaded (\"\n   692\t                                    (if status (name (:status status)) \"never asked\")\n   693\t                                    \"); (dao.space.dht/load-index \" manifest\n   694\t                                    \") loads it\")\n   695\t                               nil))])))]\n   696\t    [node (if (refused? answer)\n   697\t            {apply2/id-key id, apply2/error-key answer}\n   698\t            (apply2/success-response id (:ok answer)))]))\n   699\t\n   700\t\n   701\t(defn- dht-op?\n   702\t  [request]\n   703\t  (contains? (set (vals dht-ops)) (apply2/request-op request)))\n   704\t\n   705\t\n   706\t(defn- link-op?\n   707\t  [request]\n   708\t  (contains? (set (vals link-ops)) (apply2/request-op request)))\n   709\t\n   710\t\n   711\t(defn- session-modules\n   712\t  \"`[linked hosts]` of the requesting VM's module `registry`: the modules\n   713\t   it linked through the linker, `{name manifest-address}` -- a linked\n   714\t   entry carries its manifest's address -- and the names of its host\n   715\t   modules, which carry none.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
