{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc | sed -n '635,855p'\"","aggregated_output":"   635\t\n   636\t(defn- dht-answer\n   637\t  \"The response to one `dao.space.dht` call, answered from `node` — the\n   638\t   shell's DHT node — by the `dao.space.dht` function the operation\n   639\t   names, and the node after it: `load-index` starts a load and answers\n   640\t   its status at once, never waiting; `load-status` answers the load's\n   641\t   status map; `q` answers `dao.space.dht/q` under `limits`, refused\n   642\t   until the index is loaded; `retry` and `cancel` answer `:retrying`\n   643\t   and `:cancelled`, or the plain function's refusal; `load-module`\n   644\t   starts a closure load and answers its status, and `module-status`\n   645\t   answers it without the loaded closure.  Answers\n   646\t   `[node response]`.\"\n   647\t  [node limits request]\n   648\t  (let [id (apply2/request-id request)\n   649\t        [manifest & more] (apply2/request-args request)\n   650\t        [node answer]\n   651\t        (cond\n   652\t          (nil? node)\n   653\t          [node (unavailable (str \"the shell has no DHT node; start it with \"\n   654\t                                  \"--index-store dht:<dir> and --dht-peer\"))]\n   655\t\n   656\t          (nil? (encoded-size (apply2/request-args request)))\n   657\t          [node (invalid \"dao.space.dht takes portable Yin data only\")]\n   658\t\n   659\t          (not (jing/segment-address? manifest))\n   660\t          [node (invalid (str \"dao.space.dht expects a manifest address, got \"\n   661\t                              (pr-str manifest)))]\n   662\t\n   663\t          :else\n   664\t          (case (apply2/request-op request)\n   665\t            ::dht-load-index\n   666\t            (let [node (dht/load-index node manifest)]\n   667\t              [node {:ok (:status (dht/load-status node manifest))}])\n   668\t\n   669\t            ::dht-load-status\n   670\t            [node {:ok (host-status (dht/load-status node manifest))}]\n   671\t\n   672\t            ::dht-load-module\n   673\t            (let [node (linker.dht/load-module node manifest)]\n   674\t              [node {:ok (:status (linker.dht/module-status node manifest))}])\n   675\t\n   676\t            ::dht-module-status\n   677\t            [node {:ok (host-status (linker.dht/module-status node manifest))}]\n   678\t\n   679\t            ::dht-retry\n   680\t            (publication-call node manifest dht/retry! :retrying)\n   681\t\n   682\t            ::dht-cancel\n   683\t            (publication-call node manifest dht/cancel! :cancelled)\n   684\t\n   685\t            ::dht-q\n   686\t            (let [status (dht/load-status node manifest)\n   687\t                  [query & inputs] more]\n   688\t              [node (if (= :loaded (:status status))\n   689\t                      (bounded #(apply dht/q node manifest query inputs) limits)\n   690\t                      (refusal ::index-unavailable\n   691\t                               (str \"the index \" manifest \" is not loaded (\"\n   692\t                                    (if status (name (:status status)) \"never asked\")\n   693\t                                    \"); (dao.space.dht/load-index \" manifest\n   694\t                                    \") loads it\")\n   695\t                               nil))])))]\n   696\t    [node (if (refused? answer)\n   697\t            {apply2/id-key id, apply2/error-key answer}\n   698\t            (apply2/success-response id (:ok answer)))]))\n   699\t\n   700\t\n   701\t(defn- dht-op?\n   702\t  [request]\n   703\t  (contains? (set (vals dht-ops)) (apply2/request-op request)))\n   704\t\n   705\t\n   706\t(defn- link-op?\n   707\t  [request]\n   708\t  (contains? (set (vals link-ops)) (apply2/request-op request)))\n   709\t\n   710\t\n   711\t(defn- session-modules\n   712\t  \"`[linked hosts]` of the requesting VM's module `registry`: the modules\n   713\t   it linked through the linker, `{name manifest-address}` -- a linked\n   714\t   entry carries its manifest's address -- and the names of its host\n   715\t   modules, which carry none.\"\n   716\t  [registry]\n   717\t  (let [entries (module/module-entries registry)]\n   718\t    [(into {} (keep (fn [[n e]] (when (some? (:address e)) [n (:address e)])))\n   719\t           entries)\n   720\t     (set (keep (fn [[n e]] (when (nil? (:address e)) n)) entries))]))\n   721\t\n   722\t\n   723\t(defn- link-answer\n   724\t  \"The response to one `yin.link` call, from `node` -- the shell's DHT\n   725\t   node -- and `indexer`, the session's code indexer, under the session\n   726\t   composition `ctx` (`:authority`, `:key`, `:primitives`, `:modules`,\n   727\t   `:round`): `names` answers `yin.vm.linker.dht/names`; `publish` answers\n   728\t   `yin.vm.linker.dht/publish-name!` over the published index, whose\n   729\t   name envelopes the indexer then commits and publishes as one\n   730\t   transaction, the HEAD write announcing the round's publication.  A\n   731\t   refusal is answered under its own reason.  Answers `[node indexer\n   732\t   response]`.\"\n   733\t  [node indexer ctx request]\n   734\t  (let [id (apply2/request-id request)\n   735\t        args (apply2/request-args request)\n   736\t        [indexer answer]\n   737\t        (cond\n   738\t          (nil? node)\n   739\t          [indexer (unavailable (str \"the shell has no DHT node; start it with \"\n   740\t                                     \"--index-store dht:<dir>\"))]\n   741\t\n   742\t          (nil? (encoded-size args))\n   743\t          [indexer (invalid \"yin.link takes portable Yin data only\")]\n   744\t\n   745\t          (= ::link-names (apply2/request-op request))\n   746\t          [indexer {:ok (linker.dht/names node (:authority ctx))}]\n   747\t\n   748\t          :else\n   749\t          (let [[name exports] args\n   750\t                db (when (and (symbol? name) (sequential? exports)\n   751\t                              (every? symbol? exports))\n   752\t                     (snapshot indexer))]\n   753\t            (cond\n   754\t              (nil? db)\n   755\t              [indexer (invalid (str \"yin.link/publish expects a module name \"\n   756\t                                     \"and a vector of export names, got \"\n   757\t                                     (pr-str args)))]\n   758\t\n   759\t              (refused? db) [indexer db]\n   760\t\n   761\t              :else\n   762\t              (let [[linked hosts] (session-modules (:modules ctx))\n   763\t                    res (linker.dht/publish-name!\n   764\t                          node db {:name name\n   765\t                                   :exports (vec exports)\n   766\t                                   :key (:key ctx)\n   767\t                                   :primitives (:primitives ctx)\n   768\t                                   :modules linked\n   769\t                                   :host-modules hosts})\n   770\t                    indexer' (if (seq (:envelopes res))\n   771\t                               (repl.index/commit-names indexer (:envelopes res)\n   772\t                                                        (:round ctx))\n   773\t                               indexer)]\n   774\t                (cond\n   775\t                  (= :refused (:status res))\n   776\t                  [indexer (refusal (:reason res)\n   777\t                                    (str \"yin.link/publish refused: \"\n   778\t                                         (pr-str (dissoc res :status :reason)))\n   779\t                                    nil)]\n   780\t\n   781\t                  (not= (:failure indexer) (:failure indexer'))\n   782\t                  [indexer' (unavailable \"the name assertion was not indexed\")]\n   783\t\n   784\t                  :else\n   785\t                  [indexer'\n   786\t                   {:ok {:module name\n   787\t                         :address (:address res)\n   788\t                         :links (into {}\n   789\t                                      (map (fn [[f o]]\n   790\t                                             [f (if (= :ok (:status o))\n   791\t                                                  :ok\n   792\t                                                  (:reason o))]))\n   793\t                                      (:links res))}}])))))]\n   794\t    [node indexer (if (refused? answer)\n   795\t                    {apply2/id-key id, apply2/error-key answer}\n   796\t                    (apply2/success-response id (:ok answer)))]))\n   797\t\n   798\t\n   799\t;; =============================================================================\n   800\t;; The interpreter\n   801\t;; =============================================================================\n   802\t\n   803\t(defn serve\n   804\t  \"One serve round of the query interpreter over `pair`: answer every\n   805\t   request its cursor has not consumed, from `indexer` and `ast-indexer`\n   806\t   as they stand now, at most `budget` of them.  A response is appended before the cursor\n   807\t   moves past its request; one the call-out refuses leaves the request to\n   808\t   be re-read.  A value that is not a request envelope is consumed\n   809\t   unanswered: no call made it.  A `dao.space.dht` call is answered from\n   810\t   `dht`, the shell's DHT node, which a `load-index` advances.  A\n   811\t   `yin.link` call is answered from `dht` and `indexer` under `link`, the\n   812\t   session composition `link-answer` reads; a publish advances both.\n   813\t   Returns `{:pair pair :dht node :indexer indexer :progress? bool\n   814\t   :answered n}`, `n` the responses appended.\"\n   815\t  [{:keys [pair indexer ast-indexer dht limits budget link]}]\n   816\t  (loop [pair pair\n   817\t         node dht\n   818\t         indexer indexer\n   819\t         remaining budget\n   820\t         progress? false\n   821\t         answered 0]\n   822\t    (let [r (when (pos? remaining)\n   823\t              (stream/next (:call-in pair) (:cursor pair)))\n   824\t          done (fn [pair node indexer progress? answered]\n   825\t                 {:pair pair, :dht node, :indexer indexer,\n   826\t                  :progress? progress?, :answered answered})]\n   827\t      (if-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   828\t        (done pair node indexer progress? answered)\n   829\t        (let [request (:dao.stream/value r)\n   830\t              [node' indexer' response]\n   831\t              (cond\n   832\t                (not (apply2/request? request)) [node indexer nil]\n   833\t                (dht-op? request) (let [[n response] (dht-answer node limits request)]\n   834\t                                    [n indexer response])\n   835\t                (link-op? request) (link-answer node indexer link request)\n   836\t                :else [node indexer (answer indexer ast-indexer limits request)])\n   837\t              landed? (or (nil? response)\n   838\t                          (= :dao.stream/ok\n   839\t                             (:dao.stream/outcome\n   840\t                               (apply2/put-response! (:call-out pair)\n   841\t                                                     response))))]\n   842\t          (if landed?\n   843\t            (recur (assoc pair :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   844\t                   node'\n   845\t                   indexer'\n   846\t                   (dec remaining)\n   847\t                   true\n   848\t                   (cond-> answered response inc))\n   849\t            (done pair node indexer progress? answered)))))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc | sed -n '340,430p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc | sed -n '255,345p'\"","aggregated_output":"   340\t        (do (index/read-manifest (:content-store ix) manifest-address)\n   341\t            (when-some [write-head! (:after-publish ix)]\n   342\t              (write-head! manifest-address))\n   343\t            (assoc ix\n   344\t                   :manifest-address manifest-address\n   345\t                   :published (:transactions ix)\n   346\t                   :published-payloads n))))\n   347\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) e\n   348\t      (assoc ix\n   349\t             :failure {:round round :stage :publish :message (ex-message e)}))))\n   350\t\n   351\t\n   352\t(defn- consume\n   353\t  \"Advance the observer past every packet still on the medium, handing each\n   354\t   to `f` with the indexer; a gap marks the indexer lost, after which no\n   355\t   packet reaches `f`.\"\n   356\t  [indexer f]\n   357\t  (loop [ix indexer]\n   358\t    (let [{:keys [status batch] observer' :observer}\n   359\t          (observer/observe-next (:observer ix))\n   360\t          ix (assoc ix :observer observer')]\n   361\t      (case status\n   362\t        :ok (recur (if (:lost? ix) ix (f ix batch)))\n   363\t        :gap (recur (assoc ix :lost? true))\n   364\t        ix))))\n   365\t\n   366\t\n   367\t(defn step\n   368\t  \"The round's index step: observe every packet `program-out` still holds\n   369\t   for this observer, commit each through the round's publication, publish\n   370\t   when any was committed, then drop the publication — its transactor,\n   371\t   intake, and pool — so the indexer carries none of this round's payloads\n   372\t   into the next.  A gap is recovered across, counted on the observer's\n   373\t   `:ingress-gaps`, and marks the indexer lost: the missing packet and\n   374\t   every later one are never called indexed.\"\n   375\t  [indexer round]\n   376\t  (let [ix (consume indexer\n   377\t                    (fn [ix packet]\n   378\t                      (first (commit (open-publication ix) packet round))))\n   379\t        ;; a row this round could not put leaves the round unpublished:\n   380\t        ;; no announcement names a program whose rows are not held\n   381\t        rows-failed? (and (not= (:failure indexer) (:failure ix))\n   382\t                          (= :materialize (:stage (:failure ix))))]\n   383\t    (dissoc (if (and (> (:transactions ix) (:transactions indexer))\n   384\t                     (not rows-failed?))\n   385\t              (publish ix round)\n   386\t              ix)\n   387\t            :publication)))\n   388\t\n   389\t\n   390\t(defn commit-names\n   391\t  \"Commit the signed name envelopes `signed` -- each `{:envelope e :proof\n   392\t   p}` -- as ONE transaction, then publish the covered indexes at once,\n   393\t   the HEAD write included (docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md 6.1): one\n   394\t   entity per envelope carrying `:yin.module/envelope` and\n   395\t   `:yin.module/proof`, with the session's metadata entity -- `:db/op`,\n   396\t   the session token and `round`, no program root -- in `m`.  A\n   397\t   transaction refused is recorded as the failure, like a packet's.\"\n   398\t  [indexer signed round]\n   399\t  (let [ix (open-publication indexer)\n   400\t        meta-e (:next-e ix)\n   401\t        untimed (fn [e a v m] [e a v nil m])\n   402\t        tx-data (into [(untimed meta-e :db/op :db/assert datom/default-op)\n   403\t                       (untimed meta-e :yin.repl/session (:session-token ix)\n   404\t                                datom/default-op)\n   405\t                       (untimed meta-e :yin.repl/round round datom/default-op)]\n   406\t                      (comp (map-indexed\n   407\t                              (fn [i {:keys [envelope proof]}]\n   408\t                                (let [e (+ meta-e 1 i)]\n   409\t                                  [(untimed e :yin.module/envelope envelope meta-e)\n   410\t                                   (untimed e :yin.module/proof proof meta-e)])))\n   411\t                            cat)\n   412\t                      signed)\n   413\t        answer (transactor/transact! (get-in ix [:publication :transactor])\n   414\t                                     tx-data)]\n   415\t    (dissoc (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome answer))\n   416\t              (-> ix\n   417\t                  (assoc :next-e (+ meta-e 1 (count signed)))\n   418\t                  (update :transactions inc)\n   419\t                  (publish round))\n   420\t              (assoc ix\n   421\t                     :failure {:round round\n   422\t                               :stage :transact\n   423\t                               :outcome (:dao.stream/outcome answer)}))\n   424\t            :publication)))\n   425\t\n   426\t\n   427\t(defn skip\n   428\t  \"Advance the observer past every packet still on the medium without\n   429\t   indexing it: a round that threw before its program ran executes nothing,\n   430\t   so nothing is indexed.  A gap still marks the indexer lost.\"\n   255\t      (and module (contains? modules module))\n   256\t      [:requires module (get modules module)]\n   257\t\n   258\t      (and module (contains? (set host-modules) module))\n   259\t      (refusal :yin.link.publish/host-module {:name n :module module})\n   260\t\n   261\t      (and (nil? module) (contains? primitives n))\n   262\t      [:primitives n (vm/profile-of primitives n)]\n   263\t\n   264\t      :else (refusal :yin.link.publish/undeclared-free {:name n}))))\n   265\t\n   266\t\n   267\t(defn module-from-index\n   268\t  \"`publish-module!`'s spec for the module `name` exporting `exports`,\n   269\t   derived from the indexed code of `db` (section 5.3), or a refusal.\n   270\t   Persists nothing.\n   271\t\n   272\t   The defining program of a symbol is the indexed program of greatest\n   273\t   `t` defining it at module level.  The exports' defining programs are\n   274\t   collected, then the defining program of every free name they hold\n   275\t   that some indexed program defines, to a fixed point; the tree is the\n   276\t   collected programs in ascending `t`.  Each remaining free name is a\n   277\t   primitive of `primitives` (declared with its profile), or qualified by\n   278\t   a module of `modules` -- `{name manifest-address}`, the modules the\n   279\t   session linked -- (declared under `:requires`).  A name qualified by\n   280\t   one of `host-modules` refuses `:yin.link.publish/host-module`, any\n   281\t   other `:yin.link.publish/undeclared-free`.\"\n   282\t  [db {:keys [name exports] :as opts}]\n   283\t  (let [programs (mapv (fn [p]\n   284\t                         (assoc p\n   285\t                                :defines (definitions (:ast p))\n   286\t                                :free (free-of (:ast p))))\n   287\t                       (indexed-programs db))\n   288\t        defining (fn [sym]\n   289\t                   (last (filter #(contains? (:defines %) sym) programs)))\n   290\t        undefined (first (remove defining exports))]\n   291\t    (if undefined\n   292\t      (refusal :yin.link.publish/undefined-export {:export undefined})\n   293\t      (let [collected (loop [ms (set (map (comp :m defining) exports))]\n   294\t                        (let [ps (filterv #(contains? ms (:m %)) programs)\n   295\t                              more (into ms\n   296\t                                         (keep (comp :m defining))\n   297\t                                         (mapcat :free ps))]\n   298\t                          (if (= more ms) ps (recur more))))\n   299\t            declared (map #(free-declaration % opts)\n   300\t                          (sort-by str\n   301\t                                   (remove defining\n   302\t                                           (distinct (mapcat :free collected)))))]\n   303\t        (or (some #(when (map? %) %) declared)\n   304\t            {:name name\n   305\t             :ast (sequenced (mapv :ast collected))\n   306\t             :exports (set exports)\n   307\t             :requires (into {}\n   308\t                             (keep (fn [[k n a]] (when (= :requires k) [n a])))\n   309\t                             declared)\n   310\t             :primitives (into {}\n   311\t                               (keep (fn [[k n p]] (when (= :primitives k) [n p])))\n   312\t                               declared)})))))\n   313\t\n   314\t\n   315\t;; =============================================================================\n   316\t;; Name envelopes (6.1, 6.5, 6.6)\n   317\t;; =============================================================================\n   318\t\n   319\t(defn- signed\n   320\t  [key env e]\n   321\t  (let [proof (sign/sign-envelope (:seed key) env)\n   322\t        e (if (some? e) e -1)]\n   323\t    {:envelope env\n   324\t     :proof proof\n   325\t     :datoms [[e :yin.module/envelope env] [e :yin.module/proof proof]]}))\n   326\t\n   327\t\n   328\t(defn assertion\n   329\t  \"The assertion envelope binding `name` to the module manifest\n   330\t   `manifest` at sequence `seq`, signed by `key` (`{:seed :public}`):\n   331\t   `{:envelope e :proof p :datoms [...]}`, the datoms of entity `e`\n   332\t   (default -1) as section 6.1 indexes them.\"\n   333\t  [key {:keys [name manifest seq e]}]\n   334\t  (signed key\n   335\t          {:yin.module/op :assert\n   336\t           :yin.module/name name\n   337\t           :yin.module/manifest manifest\n   338\t           :yin.module/asserted-by (sign/principal (:public key))\n   339\t           :yin.module/seq seq}\n   340\t          e))\n   341\t\n   342\t\n   343\t(defn retraction\n   344\t  \"The retraction of the assertion whose envelope id is `of`, at\n   345\t   sequence `seq`, signed by `key`; shaped as `assertion`'s answer.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
